  "verbalization": "Excisusin C is shown to have targets that ultimately lead to Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Excisusin C acts as a modulator of VMRC-LCP, which in turn targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. Similarly, Excisusin C also interacts with HaCaT, a cell line, which is targeted by another compound, (1R,4R)-4-Hydroxydauca-7-Ene-6,9-Dione, which also targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. These findings indicate that Excisusin C may exert its effects through multiple pathways, with some of its targets being directly linked to Phosphodiesterase 6C. The evidence is consistent with the idea that Excisusin C influences cellular processes that involve Phosphodiesterase 6C, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The scores from the different paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct involvement of Excisusin C in the regulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C.",
